Author: ubehera <ubehera@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri May 29 22:29:56 2026 -0600

    [GB10][spec] Fuse EAGLE verify-sync broadcast trio into one collective (cross-node NEXTN stall)
    
    The cross-node TP=2 Qwen3.6-27B NEXTN service wedges under thinking-on load
    (temp>0, the non-greedy verify branch). rank-0 NCCL watchdog C-stack pins the
    hang at the verify-sync broadcast in EagleVerifyInput.sample()
    (eagle_info_v2.py:469, OpType=BROADCAST NumelIn=8, PG ID 2 = TP device group),
    followed by an 18-min frozen /health detok heartbeat and a collective-timeout
    process kill. The scheduler thread sits in the downstream
    process_batch_result_decode -> copy_done.synchronize() drain, which is why the
    'no response from detokenizer' health check trips -- it is a scheduler-iteration
    block, not a slow detok thread.
    
    The greedy branch (all_greedy, e.g. think-off) has no broadcast and does not
    wedge, matching the thinking-on-only symptom. The three small back-to-back
    broadcasts are the documented NCCL desync hazard ('order of collectives not the
    same / a scheduled collective didn't run'). Fuse them into ONE broadcast over a
    contiguous int32 buffer: removes the inter-broadcast desync window and cuts the
    cross-node launch cost 3x.
    
    Cross-rank symmetric (the d3433cb09 lesson): the packed buffer length derives
    only from bs + spec_steps, both byte-identical across ranks (decode batch
    delivered via broadcast_pyobj; branch gated by rank-identical is_all_greedy), so
    the single collective is issued unanimously. Feature-preserving: NEXTN k=3,
    cudagraph, mamba, multimodal untouched -- only the wire format of the existing
    sync values changes.
    
    HONESTY: root cause (this broadcast trio is the stall locus) is confirmed from
    the rank-0 watchdog C-stack + source. Whether fusion is fully curative vs a
    strong mitigation depends on rank-1's position at the stall, which the rolled
    rank-1 log did not preserve; a live dual-rank py-spy (diagnostics/
    capture-nextn-stall-dualrank.sh) should confirm before declaring closed. NOT
    built/deployed.

diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/speculative/eagle_utils.py b/python/sglang/srt/speculative/eagle_utils.py
index 21de68eb8..e41f9c1ec 100644
--- a/python/sglang/srt/speculative/eagle_utils.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/speculative/eagle_utils.py
@@ -540,9 +540,52 @@ def eagle_sample(
             get_attention_tp_group() if is_dp_attention_enabled() else get_tp_group()
         )
         if tp_group.world_size > 1:
-            tp_group.broadcast(predict, src=0)
-            tp_group.broadcast(accept_index, src=0)
-            tp_group.broadcast(num_correct_drafts, src=0)
+            # [GB10] Fuse the three verify-sync broadcasts into a single
+            # collective over one contiguous buffer.
+            #
+            # WHY: on cross-node (single-GPU-per-node) TP=2 these three small
+            # back-to-back broadcasts have hung the forward stream with an NCCL
+            # collective timeout (confirmed: rank-0 watchdog C-stack at this
+            # exact eagle_sample() -> tp_group.broadcast site, OpType=BROADCAST
+            # NumelIn=8; SeqNum enqueued 43216-43218, completed 43215; the
+            # scheduler thread then blocks forever in the downstream
+            # copy_done.synchronize() and the /health detok heartbeat trips).
+            # Three separate enqueue points on the cross-node link is exactly
+            # the "order of collectives not the same / a scheduled collective
+            # didn't run" hazard NCCL names; collapsing to ONE collective
+            # removes the inter-broadcast desync window and cuts the cross-node
+            # launch/handshake cost 3x.
+            #
+            # SYMMETRY (the d3433cb09 lesson): predict/accept_index/
+            # num_correct_drafts are all int32 and their shapes derive only
+            # from bs and the spec step count, both of which are byte-identical
+            # across ranks (the decode batch is delivered to every TP rank via
+            # broadcast_pyobj in recv_requests, and this whole branch is gated
+            # by the rank-identical sampling_info.is_all_greedy). So the packed
+            # buffer has the same length on both ranks and the single broadcast
+            # is issued unanimously -- it cannot itself introduce a divergence.
+            # Feature-preserving: NEXTN/cudagraph/mamba/multimodal untouched;
+            # this only changes HOW the existing sync values cross the wire.
+            _predict_n = predict.numel()
+            _accept_n = accept_index.numel()
+            _packed = torch.empty(
+                _predict_n + _accept_n + num_correct_drafts.numel(),
+                dtype=torch.int32,
+                device=device,
+            )
+            _packed[:_predict_n].copy_(predict.reshape(-1))
+            _packed[_predict_n : _predict_n + _accept_n].copy_(
+                accept_index.reshape(-1)
+            )
+            _packed[_predict_n + _accept_n :].copy_(num_correct_drafts)
+            tp_group.broadcast(_packed, src=0)
+            predict = _packed[:_predict_n].view_as(predict)
+            accept_index = _packed[
+                _predict_n : _predict_n + _accept_n
+            ].view_as(accept_index)
+            num_correct_drafts = _packed[
+                _predict_n + _accept_n :
+            ].view_as(num_correct_drafts)
 
     if SIMULATE_ACC_LEN > 0:
